catalog parsed: 58 clusters, 22680 Hectospec + 2621 literature galaxies = 25301
assigned members: 10145 (paper total: 10,145); Np sum = 10479 (uniques + 334 two-cluster overlaps; paper states 334)

====================================================================================================
PART 2 -- THE CATALOG SPEC
====================================================================================================
  per-cluster assigned n_mem vs published Nm: median diff 0, mean -4.2
  r/R500 coverage (critical window 2-5 R500): clusters reaching R>=2: 58/58; >=3: 58/58; >=4: 57/58; >=5: 55/58;  members at R>=2: 5668, in [2,5]: 3629; clusters with >=12 members in-window: 58/58
  v_los errors: per-galaxy e_cz (table2/3; median across members 36 km/s; paper: rvsao internal errors ~56 km/s absorption / 21 km/s emission); jackknife per-bin errors reported in the first-use bins below.
  interloper treatment (as published): Diaferio & Geller 1999 / Diaferio 1999 caustic technique with q=25 adaptive-kernel smoothing; membership = position INSIDE the caustics (Np flag in table2/3; Np=0 non-member, Np>=1 member of N clusters).  G195's estimator adds its own iterative 3.5-sigma MAD cleaning before binning.  Caveat: the caustic envelope itself is the interloper boundary at 2-5 R500 -- outer bins contain caustic-selected (virial + infall) members, not interloper-free equilibrium tracers.
  FIT CATALOG: all 58 HeCS clusters reach the critical window with >=12 in-window members -> fit catalog = 58 clusters (the full HeCS set); 50/58 reach 5 R500.
  stack normalization: M500_med = 2.405 x1e14 Msun (caustic M200 -> NFW c500=4.5, the G195 mass model), R500_med = 0.700 Mpc (h^-1; ratio units h-independent); r200/r500 med = 1.493

====================================================================================================
PART 3 -- THE FIRST-USE: G195's executable on the HeCS members
====================================================================================================
  PRIMARY (nearest-center assignment, 10145 members of 58 clusters):
    beta_win(2-5 R500) = 0.434 +- 0.015   (boot mean 0.434, n_boot 60)
    fitted (beta_inf, r_a) = (1.225, 4.360 R500), chi2 = 805.6
    binned sigma_los(R): R=0.29: 813+-42 km/s (n=216); R=0.41: 938+-33 km/s (n=314); R=0.56: 939+-27 km/s (n=485); R=0.78: 957+-23 km/s (n=680); R=1.08: 857+-19 km/s (n=849); R=1.50: 779+-16 km/s (n=1084); R=2.08: 726+-14 km/s (n=1188); R=2.88: 630+-12 km/s (n=1307); R=3.99: 543+-11 km/s (n=1287); R=5.52: 459+-9 km/s (n=1059)
  SCORING: vs static null 0: z = 29.7 sigma; vs streaming rule 0.5: z = -4.5 sigma; vs streaming window-mean 0.594: z = -10.9 sigma; precision gate sigma<=0.167: PASS (sigma = 0.015)
  SENSITIVITY (0.525 deg field cut, 9384 members): beta_win = 0.432 +- 0.015

